        "timestamp": 1776336161,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. China condemns US Hormuz blockade as oil flows Disrupted Issued on: 16/04/2026 - 12:42 In 2025 China imported 5.4 million barrels of crude oil through the Strait of Hormuz every day, making it one of the waterway's largest stakeholders. As the economic effects of the US blockade of the strait reach China's shores, Beijing has condemned the move as \"dangerous and irresponsible\". Meanwhile, Donald Trump claimed on Wednesday that he is working with Beijing, and that China welcomed his efforts to reopen the waterway. Netanyahu will speak with Lebanese president Aoun, Israeli minister says 16/04/2026 Pope urges Cameroon's leaders to examine 'conscience', tackle corruption 16/04/2026 French MPs to debate antisemitism law that critics say will stifle criticism 16/04/2026 France father who confined son in van faces 30 years in jail 16/04/2026 Pakistani army chief visits Tehran in hopes for renewed talks between US and Iran 16/04/2026 Ukraine: At least 16 killed in overnight Russian strikes 16/04/2026 Madonna announces new album, a sequel two decades later, 'Confessions on a Dance Floor: Part II' 16/04/2026 Trump says Lebanese and Israeli leaders to speak 16/04/2026 Lebanon expresses cautious optimism on US president's claim of direct talks with Israel 16/04/2026"
